# Identifiers that must never appear in tracked files or git history.
# Derived from the samples/ audit (git history leaks + real environment).
# Covers ALL identifier forms per the adcs-lens WI-010 lesson:
# hostnames, AD domain, email, personal name, GitHub username — not just hostnames.
#
# This file is gitignored (.identifiers-denylist.local) and never committed.
# In CI it comes from the REGISTA_FORBIDDEN_IDENTIFIERS repo secret.

# --- Hostnames (NetBIOS / short) ---
mvmcitest01
mvmpostgres01

# --- AD domain (DNS) ---
hraedon.com

# --- GitHub username (appears in noreply email + GitHub paths) ---
# NOTE: 'hraedon' alone is too broad for the working-tree gate (matches
# github.com/hraedon/... URLs in README, docs, CI). It IS needed for the
# history scrub — see scripts/filter-repo-replacements.txt. The working-tree
# gate catches the email form (plm@hraedon.com) which is the real concern;
# the broad 'hraedon' replacement is handled by the filter-repo scrub.
# hraedon

# --- Email ---
plm@hraedon.com

# --- Personal name (surname only — first name too generic) ---
Merritt